<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.5.1: Analyzing Graphs of Linear Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00128</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.5.1: Analyzing Graphs of Linear Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5e207617-e606-44c5-ac46-eeb939e7bf91</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Which one doesn’t belong?</para>
          <table class="unnumbered" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="4">
            
  <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>A.<newline/>
                    <media alt="Line graph with x-axis labeled hours and y-axis labeled dollars; a straight line rises diagonally from the origin, showing a positive linear relationship between hours and dollars.">
                      <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_02_01.svg"/>
                    </media></entry>
                  <entry>B.<newline/>
                    <media alt="A simple line graph with hours labeled on the y-axis and dollars on the x-axis. The line slopes upward, showing hours increasing as dollars increase.">
                      <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_02_02.svg"/>
                    </media></entry>
                  <entry> C.<newline/>
                    <media alt="A graph with hours on the x-axis and dollars on the y-axis shows a dotted upward-sloping line, indicating an increase in dollars as hours increase.">
                      <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_02_03.svg"/>
                    </media></entry>
                  <entry>D.<newline/>
                    <media alt="A line graph with dollars on the vertical axis and hours on the horizontal axis. The line slopes downward, indicating that as hours increase, dollars decrease.">
                      <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_02_04.svg"/>
                    </media></entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some sample responses:</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>A is the only graph that intersects the vertical axis at 0 (or that starts at the origin).</item>
            <item>B is the only graph where the horizontal axis represents dollars and the vertical axis represents hours.</item>
            <item>C is the only graph that is discrete, showing plotted points (that lie along a line) instead of a continuous line.</item>
            <item>D is the only graph with a negative slope (or that slants downward from left to right).</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
